{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Text Images Grid",
  "tag": "div",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "TYPES OF CACAO"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "bottom_heading",
      "label": "Bottom Heading",
      "default": "WHY CHUNCHO?"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "bottom_description",
      "label": "Bottom Description",
      "default": "<p>Ceremonial Chuncho cacao from Peru embodies the essence of ancient traditions, cultivated by indigenous farmers with reverence for their land. Mainly wild harvested, this exquisite cacao variety boasts a rich cocoa butter content from being grown at higher elevation. It gives subtle notes of Andean fruit, offering a sensory journey steeped with history and authenticity. </p><p>Its origins date back centuries, when it was grown by the Machiguenga indigenous communities in the Amazon basin since pre Inca civilization periods Wild harvested Chuncho cacao ensures the preservation of the biodiverse species of plants in the forests and jungles of Peru.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "grid_item",
      "name": "Grid Item",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "image",
          "label": "Image"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "Title",
          "default": "chuncho"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "description",
          "label": "Description",
          "default": "<p>Chuncho cacao is a uniquely sought-after variety, offering a rare blend of exquisite flavors like floral, fruit, and nuts. Its heirloom genetic diversity, and sustainable cultivation practices are what gives its status among other varieties. Some call chuncho \"the best criollo\"</p>"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Text Images Grid",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "grid_item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "chuncho",
            "description": "<p>Chuncho cacao is a uniquely sought-after variety, offering a rare blend of exquisite flavors like floral, fruit, and nuts. Its heirloom genetic diversity, and sustainable cultivation practices are what gives its status among other varieties. Some call chuncho \"the best criollo\"</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "grid_item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "forastero",
            "description": "<p>Forastero cacao, prevalent in Africa and essential for mass-produced chocolate, faces challenges related to labor and sustainablity practices, and provides a more uniform and less complex flavor than the rich and varied profiles of premium varieties like Chuncho</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "grid_item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "CRIOLLO",
            "description": "<p>Criollo cacao, celebrated for its complex flavors and one of the worlds best cacao varieties, faces sustainability challenges due to its limited genetic diversity from cloning. Generally it is thought to be prestigious of all the varieties of cacao for its rich flavors and high health benefits </p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "grid_item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "TRINITARIO",
            "description": "<p>Trinitario cacao, a non-heirloom hybrid developed from Criollo and Forastero varieties, combines the robustness of Forastero with the refined flavors of Criollo, offering a balanced and complex flavor profile that is highly valued in chocolate production.</p>"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}